(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ce-easy-2026-014"]={"v":1,"id":"ce-easy-2026-014","title":"Full Syllabus Test-5 2026 ESE CE General Studies & Engineering Aptitude","sourceTitle":"Full Syllabus Test-5 2026 ESE CE General Studies & Engineering Aptitude","branch":"CIVIL ENGINEERING","code":"CE","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering","seriesId":"ce-easy-2026","num":14,"category":"aptitude","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":7200,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering • Questions: 100","package":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering"},"source":"CIVIL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering/017_Full Syllabus Test-5 2026 ESE CE General Studies & Engineering Aptitude.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding India-Russia Relations:<br />\n1. Russia was India’s largest crude oil supplier in FY 2024–25.<br />\n2. Exercise INDRA is a bilateral military exercise between India and Russia.<br />\n3. India’s bilateral trade with Russia is export-dominated, led by pharmaceuticals and textiles.<br />\n<strong>Which of the above statements is/are correct?</strong></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nIndia&rsquo;s bilateral trade with Russia is import-dominated, led by crude oil.</p>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to the Industrial Park Rating System (IPRS) 3.0, consider the following statements:<br />\n1. It has been developed by the Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT) with support from the Asian Development Bank (ADB).<br />\n2. Parameters such as sustainability, green infrastructure, logistics connectivity, digitalization, and skill linkages have been newly included in the framework.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; The Industrial Park Rating System (IPRS) 3.0 is a new upgraded framework introduced by<br />\nthe Department for Promotion of Industry and Internal Trade (DPIIT) with support from the<br />\nAsian Development Bank (ADB) to benchmark and improve the quality of industrial parks<br />\nand estates across India.<br />\n&bull; IPRS 3.0 expands on previous versions by including new, forward-looking parameters that<br />\nreflect the evolving needs of industries and sustainability goals:<br />\n&diams; <strong>Sustainability and Green Infrastructure:</strong> This includes criteria related to environmental<br />\nmanagement, energy efficiency, water conservation, waste management, and pollution<br />\ncontrol, ensuring industrial parks adopt eco-friendly practices.<br />\n&diams; <strong>Logistics Connectivity:</strong> Measures the connectivity of the park in terms of road, rail, air,<br />\nand port access, providing industries situated there with efficient supply chain and<br />\ndistribution options.<br />\n&diams; <strong>Digitalization:</strong> Emphasizes adoption of digital technologies for park management,<br />\nservices, and operations, enhancing efficiency and transparency.<br />\n&diams; <strong>Skill Linkages:</strong> Focuses on the availability and development of skilled labor within and<br />\naround the park, ensuring industries have access to the talent pool they need.</p>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to the National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF), consider the following statements:<br />\n1. NIRF was launched in 2015 by the Ministry of Education, to rank the institutions of higher education in India.<br />\n2. In 2025, the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT), Madras, claimed the top overall position in the rankings.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>‘Tondon Committee’ is related to which of the following?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"‘Tondon Committee’ is related to which of the following?"},{"key":"B","html":"Credit management and working capital finance for industries."},{"key":"C","html":"Public sector disinvestment and restructuring."},{"key":"D","html":"Establishment of the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB)."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nRecently, the Crime in India 2023 report was published by the National Crime Records Bureau<br />\n(NCRB).<br />\n<strong>About NCRB</strong><br />\n&bull; <strong>Establishment:</strong> 1986 on recommendations of the Tandon Committee, National Police<br />\nCommission (1977-81), and MHA Task Force (1985).<br />\n&bull; <strong>Parent Ministry:</strong> Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA).<br />\n<strong>&bull; Functions:</strong><br />\n&diams; Acts as the national repository of crime and criminal data.<br />\n&diams; Manages the Crime and Criminal Tracking Network &amp; Systems (CCTNS).<br />\n&diams; Publishes three major reports: Crime in India, Accidental Deaths &amp; Suicides, and Prison<br />\nStatistics.</p>"},{"n":5,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The term SAMBHAV, recently seen in the news, refers to:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"A digital grievance redressal platform of the Ministry of Education"},{"key":"B","html":"An indigenous secure mobile communication platform of the Indian Army"},{"key":"C","html":"A rural skill development initiative under the Ministry of Rural Development"},{"key":"D","html":"A satellite-based navigation system developed by ISRO"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&bull; Army Chief General Upendra Dwivedi recently highlighted the importance of SAMBHAV<br />\n(Secure Army Mobile Bharat Version).<br />\n&bull; Launched in 2023, SAMBHAV is India&rsquo;s first fully indigenous secure mobile communication<br />\nplatform, built to function independently of network infrastructure vulnerabilities.</p>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to the ‘Promotion and Regulation of Online Gaming Act, 2025’, consider the following statements:<br />\n1. It bans all real money games (RMGs), regardless of whether they are skill-based or chancebased.<br />\n2. It makes a clear legal distinction between games of skill and games of chance.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\n&bull; Recently, the Parliament of India has passed the &lsquo;Promotion and Regulation of Online Gaming<br />\nAct, 2025&rsquo;, to regulate and prohibit certain gaming formats having social and economic concerns.<br />\n&bull; The Promotion and Regulation of Online Gaming Act, 2025 bans all real money games (RMGs),<br />\nregardless of whether they are skill-based or chance-based. It prohibits advertising of real<br />\nmoney games, especially those involving monetary stakes.<br />\n&bull; The Act does not distinguish between skill and chance; eroding the legal precedent and<br />\npotentially violating Article 19(1)(g), which protects the right to trade and occupation.</p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to the Registrar General of India (RGI), consider the following statements:<br />\n1. The RGI was established in 1961 and functions under the Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation.<br />\n2. It is responsible for conducting the decennial Census of India, which has been held regularly since 1951.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; The Registrar General of India (RGI) recently asked States to take steps towards achieving universal registration of births and deaths.<br />\n&bull; The Registrar General of India (RGI) was established in 1961 by the Government of India.<br />\n&bull; It works under the administrative control of the Ministry of Home Affairs (MHA).<br />\n&bull; It conducts the decennial Census of India (since 1872; regular since 1881) and is responsible<br />\nfor planning, coordinating, and supervising census operations.</p>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Loyalty to companies or their owner should be equated with merely obeying ones’s immediate supervisor.<br />\n2. An engineer might have professional obligation to both an employer and to the public that reinforce rather than contradict each other.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nLoyalty to companies or their owner should not be equated with merely obeying ones&rsquo;s immediate<br />\nsupervisor. Hence statement 1 is incorrect.</p>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding Human values:<br />\n1. Value refers to the relative worth of a quality or object.<br />\n2. Value is what makes something desirable or undesirable.<br />\n3. What we value, guides not only our personal choices but also our perception of the worth of others.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding Utilitarian approach to ethics:<br />\n1. It is concerned with maximising the benefit and minimising the harm that arises from our decisions.<br />\n2. It motivates individual to act in a particular way.<br />\n3. It is concerned with the consequences of our decisions.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nUtilitarianism is an ethical theory that determines right from wrong by focusing on outcomes. It<br />\nis a form of consequentialism. Utilitarianism holds that the most ethical choice is the one that<br />\nwill produce the greatest good for the greatest number.</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following correctly describes the word ‘Nepotism’?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Undermining the morale of employee"},{"key":"B","html":"Being autocratic in decision-making"},{"key":"C","html":"Hiring friends and relatives for work"},{"key":"D","html":"Harassment of women employee"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nNepotism is the unfair use of power in order to get jobs or other benefits for your family or friends.</p>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following theories primarily focuses on moral character of the decision maker?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Virtue Ethics"},{"key":"B","html":"Fidelity"},{"key":"C","html":"Utilitarianism"},{"key":"D","html":"Plagiarism"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nVirtue ethics is an approach to ethics that emphasizes an individual&rsquo;s character as the key element of ethical thinking.</p>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following are behaviours exhibited by a moral person?<br />\n1. Being insensitive<br />\n2. Having a closed mindset<br />\n3. Doing the right thing<br />\nSelect the correct answer using the codes given below:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Knowledge is information of which someone is not aware.<br />\n2. Wisdom is the ability to make correct judgments and decisions.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":15,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding Ecotone:<br />\n1. Ecotone is a zone of junction between two or more diverse ecosystems.<br />\n2. Ecotone is always smaller than a biome.<br />\n3. A well-developed ecotone may contain some unique organisms which might be absent in the adjacent ecosystems.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n&bull; Ecotone is a zone of junction between two or more diverse ecosystems. For example, the<br />\nmangrove forests represent an ecotone between marine and terrestrial ecosystem.<br />\n&bull; It may be very narrow or quite wide, but smaller than a biome which is a much larger entity.<br />\n&bull; Well-developed ecotones contain some organisms which are entirely different from that of<br />\nthe adjoining communities.</p>"},{"n":16,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following steps is/are involved in the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA)?<br />\n1. Project screening<br />\n2. Identification of key impacts<br />\n3. Prediction of impacts<br />\nSelect the correct answer using the codes given below:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":17,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is not related to ozone layer protection?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Kigali Agreement"},{"key":"B","html":"Montreal Protocol"},{"key":"C","html":"Vienna Convention"},{"key":"D","html":"Basel Convention"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nThe Basel Convention is an international treaty that focuses on the control of transboundary<br />\nmovements of hazardous wastes and their disposal. The Basel Convention was adopted in 1989.</p>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Dissolved oxygen escapes the water body through the air-water interface.<br />\n2. It also escapes through respiration of organisms.<br />\n3. Oxygen is less soluble in warm water.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":19,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In which of the following phenomenon certain phytoplankton species contain pigments and bloom such that the human eye perceives the water to be discoloured?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Water toxicity"},{"key":"B","html":"Water turbidity"},{"key":"C","html":"Red Tide"},{"key":"D","html":"Eutrophication"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe phenomenon where phytoplankton species contain pigments and bloom, causing the water<br />\nto appear discoloured to the human eye is called a &ldquo;Harmful Algal Bloom&rdquo; (HAB)&rdquo;, commonly<br />\nknown as the &ldquo;Red Tide&rdquo;.</p>"},{"n":20,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is/are the type of Coral Reef?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Fringing Reef"},{"key":"B","html":"Barrier Reef"},{"key":"C","html":"Atoll Reef"},{"key":"D","html":"All of the above"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>"},{"n":21,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements about Reducing Emissions from Deforestation and Forest Degradation (REDD):<br />\n1. REDD is a collaborative program of Food and Agricultural Organization (FAO), United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) & United Nations Environment Programme.<br />\n2. REDD+ is a financing model negotiated under the UNFCCC to reduce greenhouse gas emissions from deforestation and forest degradation in developing countries.<br />\n3. REDD+ is a legally binding climate mitigation path.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1 and 3 only"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nREDD+ is a voluntary climate mitigation path.</p>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. According to India State of Forest Report 2023, the total forest and tree cover of the country is 24.62 percent of the geographical area of the country.<br />\n2. As compared to the assessment of 2021, there is an increase in the total forest and tree cover of the country.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&bull; According to the India State of Forest Report (ISFR), 2023, the total forest and tree cover of the country is 25.17% of the geographical area of the country.<br />\n&bull; As compared to the assessment of ISFR 2021, there has been an increase in the total forest and tree cover of the country, as reported in the ISFR 2023. The total forest and tree cover increased from 24.62% in 2021 to 25.17% in 2023.</p>"},{"n":23,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following are chemical processes that convert biomass to useful products?<br />\n1. Gasification<br />\n2. Biomethanation<br />\n3. Incineration<br />\nSelect the correct answer using the codes given below:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nIncineration is not considered a chemical process that converts biomass to useful products because it primarily burns biomass to generate heat, essentially destroying the biomass rather than converting it into a useful product.</p>"},{"n":24,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Oxides of Nitrogen damage the leaves of plants and retard the rate of photosynthesis.<br />\n2. They are toxic to living tissues also.<br />\n3. They are harmful to various textile fibres and metals.<br />\nWhich of the above statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nOxides of Nitrogen damage plant leaves, are toxic to living tissues, and are harmful to various textile fibers and metals.</p>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. In grassland ecosystems, the producers which are mainly grasses are always maximum in number.<br />\n2. In the pond ecosystem, the pyramid is inverted.<br />\n3. Ecological Efficiency refers to the percentage of energy transferred from one trophic level to another.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"2 and 3 only"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nIn the pond ecosystem, the pyramid is upright.</p>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements :<br />\n1. Dynamic Random-Access Memory (DRAM) is slower than Static Random-Access Memory (SRAM).<br />\n2. Cache and Memory Registers are part of Central Processing Unit (CPU), while Regular Random- Access Memory (RAM) is not its part.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; In SRAM, flip-flop circuit is used to store the data which can be accessed almost instantly<br />\nwhereas DRAM uses a capacitor to store data which requires constant refreshing to maintain<br />\nthe charge on the capacitor. Thus, Dynamic Random-Access Memory (DRAM) is slower than<br />\nStatic Random-Access Memory (SRAM).<br />\n&bull; Cache and Memory Registers are part of Central Processing Unit (CPU), while Regular Random-<br />\nAccess Memory (RAM) and Hard Disk are not its part. It acts as temporary storage area that<br />\nis more readily available to the processor than the computer&rsquo;s main memory source i.e. RAM<br />\nor ROM.</p>"},{"n":27,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>“It is a form of attack in which attacker has unauthorized access to the targeted mobile devices, laptops via Bluetooth connection by which attacker can steal photos, contacts, SMS etc.” What is described here?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Bluesnarfing"},{"key":"B","html":"Phishing"},{"key":"C","html":"Rootkit"},{"key":"D","html":"Pharming"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nBluesnarfing is a type of cyberattack that exploits Bluetooth technology to access sensitive<br />\ninformation stored on a device without the owner&#39;s knowledge or consent.</p>"},{"n":28,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is NOT a key feature of the National e-Governance plan?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Common support infrastructure"},{"key":"B","html":"Public-private Partnership"},{"key":"C","html":"Physical services"},{"key":"D","html":"Centralized initiative, decentralized implementation"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nNational e-Governance plan (NeGP) aims to make all government services accessible to Indian<br />\ncitizens via electronic media.</p>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Hyper-Text Markup Language (HTML) is basically used to design:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Tables and frames"},{"key":"B","html":"Web page"},{"key":"C","html":"Graphics"},{"key":"D","html":"Audio clip"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nHTML is the standard markup language for creating web pages and web applications.</p>"},{"n":30,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following types of software:<br />\n1. Search engines<br />\n2. Operating system<br />\n3. Game engines<br />\nWhich of the above software can be classified as system software?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nSystem Software is the software that is directly related to coordinating computer operations and<br />\nperforms tasks associated with controlling and utilizing computer hardware. These programs<br />\nassist in running application programs and are designed to control the operation of a computer<br />\nsystem. A search engine is an application software and not system software that is designed to<br />\ncarry out web searches. Hence, option (b) is correct.</p>"},{"n":31,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Cloud computing is the on-demand availability of computer system resources.<br />\n2. Virtualization is a cloud computing technique, which allows the sharing of a single physical instance of an application or resource among multiple organizations or tenants (customers).<br />\n3. Utility computing is a cloud computing technique based on the Pay-per-Use model.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nCloud Computing provides means of accessing the applications as utilities over the Internet.<br />\nUtility computing is a subset of cloud computing, where computing resources are provided on<br />\ndemand based on the Pay-per-Use model. Virtualization in cloud computing allows multiple<br />\noperating systems and applications to run simultaneously on the same hardware, which allows<br />\nthe sharing of a single physical instance of an application or resource among multiple organizations<br />\nor tenant. Hence, all the given statements are correct.</p>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. The Digital Locker provides citizens with a shareable private space on a public cloud and makes all documents/certificates available on this cloud itself.<br />\n2. Apart from e-documents, DigiLocker can store a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) link of edocuments issued by various issuer departments.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":33,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>What is the side view of given orthographic view?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/02/02bc6bcce9670f2a34f9.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c3348469fbb3d1729256.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/12/128839b3cfaefcf12460.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/07/0781eaf229f56722760c.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2bc25a4c7817c7e452fa.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c9/c98e9d68ce8f0484ccf9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":34,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If line AB of 50 mm is parallel to HP then its length in the top view is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"50 mm"},{"key":"B","html":"Less than 50 mm"},{"key":"C","html":"Point"},{"key":"D","html":"Does not seen"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nA line is parallel to some plane then its true length will be seen on that plane.</p>"},{"n":35,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A right circular cone with radius <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/b8/b82a4fd31b27ef73a290.png\" /> times of height is lying on one of its generators on HP such a way that top view of axis is parallel to VP. Find the length of semi-minor axis of ellipse in profile view. (<em>d</em> = diameter)</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"d/2"},{"key":"B","html":"d/3"},{"key":"C","html":"d/5"},{"key":"D","html":"d/4"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9e/9e4038d31989f84c8ee0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is useful contributor to a strategy of mass customization?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Modular design"},{"key":"B","html":"Off shoring"},{"key":"C","html":"Economics of sale"},{"key":"D","html":"Fixed automation"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nModular design is a design approach that subdivides a system into smaller parts that can be<br />\nindependently created and then used in different systems. This allows designs to be customized,<br />\nupgraded, repaired and for parts to be reused.</p>"},{"n":37,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which type of modularity exists when a family of dissimilar products uses the same assembly or component?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Component sharing modularity"},{"key":"B","html":"Cut to fit modularity"},{"key":"C","html":"Component swapping modularity"},{"key":"D","html":"Platform modularity"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\n<strong>Component sharing modularity:</strong> Family of dissimilar products uses the same assembly or components.<br />\n<strong>Cut to fit modularity:</strong> A component parameters or features can be adjusted to provide a variety of products.<br />\n<strong>Component swapping modularity:</strong> Modularity in a product that is differentiated only by a single component/assembly.<br />\n<strong>Platform modularity: </strong>Products that consists of different combination of modules assembled on a same basic structure.</p>"},{"n":38,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is an example of passive fire protection system?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Sprinkler"},{"key":"B","html":"Fire hydrant"},{"key":"C","html":"Fire proof cladding"},{"key":"D","html":"Stand pipe"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nPassive fire protection system is an integral component of structural fire protection and fire<br />\nsafety in a building. They does not require any action or motion in order to work in the event of fire.<br />\n<strong>Example:</strong> Fire resistance wall, fire resistant glass, closures, fire proof cladding etc.</p>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>CDM regarding safety at work stands for</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Control of demolition and management regulations."},{"key":"B","html":"Control of dangerous material regulations."},{"key":"C","html":"Construction demolition management."},{"key":"D","html":"Construction design and management regulations."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nThe CDM regulation imposes duties to manage construction project, ensure physical safeguards<br />\nare provided to prevent danger during such projects.</p>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding Cost of Conformance:<br />\n1. It is cost associated with a process not operating according to the requirement.<br />\n2. It is further divided into Prevention cost and Appraisal cost.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nCost of non conformance is the cost associated with a process not operating according to the requirement.</p>"},{"n":41,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to quality circles, consider the following statements:<br />\n1. It is a group of workers who voluntarily meet to discuss ways of improving products or process.<br />\n2. Quality circles originated in Japan.<br />\n3. The working staffs involved in quality circles meet frequently either at someone’s home or at the plant before shift begins.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"1, 2 and 3"},{"key":"C","html":"2 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1 and 3 only"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nQuality circles originated in Japan. It is a group of workers who voluntarily meet to discuss ways<br />\nof improving products or process. Quality circles are usually less structured and more informal<br />\nthan task forces entrusted with a project. The working staffs involved in quality circles meet<br />\nfrequently either at someone&rsquo;s home or at the plant before shift begins.</p>"},{"n":42,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>With reference to Cause and effect Diagram, consider the following statements<br />\n1. It studies a problem condition or improvement opportunity to find its cause and effects.<br />\n2. It enables a team to focus on the history of problem rather than on the root causes of the problem.<br />\n3. It creates a snapshot of collective knowledge and consensus of a team.<br />\nWhich of the following statements given above is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"3 only"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nCause and effect diagram enables a team to focus on the root causes of the problem rather than on the history of the problem.</p>"},{"n":43,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following pairs :</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5c/5cbea37cc4dffe824a86.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the above pairs is/are correctly matched?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"D","html":"2 only"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nnp-chart follows Binomial distribution.</p>"},{"n":44,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In a single sampling plan<br />\nN = 200 (Lot size)<br />\nn = 10 (Sample size)<br />\nc = 2 (Acceptance number)<br />\nActual defective found by inspection is 3 then the decision will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Acceptance lot"},{"key":"B","html":"Reject the lot"},{"key":"C","html":"Take 2<sup>nd</sup> sample"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nBecause number of defective is greater than acceptance number.</p>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following pairs:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/93e28baa4cf47c3776cc.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the above pair is/are correctly matched?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"3 only"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nISO 14064 - Greenhouse gases<br />\nISO 14063 - Environmental communication<br />\nISO 19011 - Guideline for auditing management system</p>"},{"n":46,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following ISO Standard provide guidance on the evaluation of competence of individuals involved in the audit process?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"ISO 19011 : 2011"},{"key":"B","html":"ISO 9001 : 2015"},{"key":"C","html":"ISO : 14000"},{"key":"D","html":"ISO 9004 : 2009"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following product quality management processes ensures that the end product conforms to functional requirements at a particular stage of construction?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Quality planning"},{"key":"B","html":"Quality assurance"},{"key":"C","html":"Quality inspection"},{"key":"D","html":"Quality audit"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; Quality planning aims at identifying the quality requirements and standards that are relevant<br />\nto the product and documenting methods for determining, how the project will conform to<br />\nthese requirements and standards.<br />\n&bull; Quality assurance focuses on demonstrating the planned and systematic confidence building<br />\nmeasures, to ensure that the necessary quality requirements and standards are being met in<br />\npractice.<br />\n&bull; Quality control is the operational technique of monitoring and recording the results of<br />\nexecution to assess performance and make necessary changes in processes (where required)<br />\nto ensure conformance to the requirements and standards.<br />\n&bull; Quality inspection determines the acceptability of the end product or deliverable or service<br />\nor a stage of construction, to ensure that it conforms to functional requirements.<br />\n&bull; Quality audit is the in-house or third party&rsquo;s systematic and independent examination and<br />\ndocumentation to determine whether product quality activities and related results comply<br />\nwith the planned arrangements and are implemented effectively to achieve project objectives.</p>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Non-availability of antivirus software, server breakdown and incompatibility of software with purchased hardware are examples of:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Technology risks"},{"key":"B","html":"Communication and network failure risks"},{"key":"C","html":"Organisational risks"},{"key":"D","html":"Cost overrun risks"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n<strong>Cost overrun risks:</strong> Inaccurate cost estimates, inadequate cost planning and control, no extra<br />\nwork control, no analysis of constantly changing market conditions, and incomplete project closure.<br />\n<strong>Technology risks:</strong> Inadequate information on new technology, non-replacement of old technology,<br />\nnon-availability of competent and professional staff to use new technology, and lack of managerial<br />\nskills.<br />\n<strong>Organisational risks:</strong> Inappropriate organisation network, poor assignment/allocation of tasks<br />\nand responsibilities, lack of competent persons, no project manual/documented procedures, project<br />\nbeing too complex for the resources available, inadequate communications infrastructure, wrong<br />\nselection of project management, no database, inflexible meetings, inability to take timely corrective<br />\naction, and incomplete project closure.<br />\n<strong>Communication and network failure risks:</strong> Non-availability of antivirus software to safeguard<br />\noffice computers, loss of data due to network breakdown, no back up of data available, vendors<br />\nnot competent enough, landline phones not working properly, lack of resources, high electricity<br />\nfluctuations, internet servers breakdown, installation of wrong computer equipment, noncompatibility<br />\nof software with the purchased hardware, and ineffective information management<br />\nsystem.</p>"},{"n":49,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In a project network (AOA), which of the following is/are incorrect?<br />\n1. All arrows must run from left to right.<br />\n2. Events should be represented by lines.<br />\n3. Two activities cannot end at the same event.<br />\n4. Arrows running close should be avoided by repositioning.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2 and 4 only"},{"key":"D","html":"2 and 3 only"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":50,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>In heuristic rules for resource allocation in context to resource smoothing, when more jobs compete for the same resource, priority is given to:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Jobs with maximum duration"},{"key":"B","html":"Jobs on the critical path only"},{"key":"C","html":"Jobs with least float"},{"key":"D","html":"Jobs that start later in the project"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe essential rules are:<br />\n1. The resources are to be allocated serially in time i.e., resource allocation should start on the<br />\nfirst day; all possible jobs are to be scheduled for the first day before moving to the second<br />\nday and so on.<br />\n2. When more jobs compete for the same resource, preference is to be given to the job/jobs with<br />\nleast float.<br />\n3. Jobs once started should continue till they are finished i.e., breaking of jobs is not allowed.<br />\n4. Whenever possible, non-critical jobs are to be postponed so that critical jobs can be scheduled<br />\nwithout increasing the project completion time.</p>"},{"n":51,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The Letter of Intent in contracting:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"is a legally binding document equivalent to contract agreement."},{"key":"B","html":"obliges the successful tenderer to immediately start work."},{"key":"C","html":"is not a legal document but indicates acceptance of offer."},{"key":"D","html":"is a letter listing intentions of owner."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThis is a letter issued to the successful tenderer intimating about his/her offer being accepted.<br />\nLOI is issued before signing of the contract by the two parties. The successful tenderer is required<br />\nto intimate any pre-condition within the stipulated time. Issue of LOI by the project promoters<br />\nand acceptance of the same by the successful tenderer does not obviate the need for signing a<br />\ncontract. Since LOI is not a legal document, the two parties have to necessarily execute the contract<br />\nby signing the contract agreement.</p>"},{"n":52,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which clause is introduced in contracts to deduct payments for unscheduled delays in work completion?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Performance bond"},{"key":"B","html":"Liquidated damages"},{"key":"C","html":"Earnest money deposit"},{"key":"D","html":"Mobilization advance"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":53,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Who among the following are the stakeholders of a construction project?</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/17/17604ac5700ac546e2f7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Select the correct answer using the codes given below:</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1, 2 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2, 3 and 4"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\nFollowing are the stakeholders of a construction project :<br />\nArchitect, Client (owner), Constructor, Engineering (consultant), Subcontractor/Supplier/Vendor,<br />\nLawyer, Insurer etc.</p>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>What is the present value of a sum of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d60b029ce96a4703d8ad.png\" /> to be received after 5 years from now by compounding semi-annually at an interest rate of 14%?</p>\n\n<p>[Take 1.07<sup>5</sup> = 1.40]</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c3/c39c2ddb628a5b154b55.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/7313ff8775b3567fe7ec.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dc4b3e8090b74d578aea.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/76/76fd3f2ae9c6b12a6f50.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb39f375c0b7876a5cf1.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The primary risk taker in a project is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Project manager"},{"key":"B","html":"Portfolio manager"},{"key":"C","html":"Project sponsor"},{"key":"D","html":"Operation manager"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe APMBok (Association of project managers body of knowledge) defines the project sponsor as,<br />\n(i) Individual or body for whom the project is undertaken, the primary risk taker.<br />\n(ii) The individual representing the sponsoring body and to whom the project manager reports.<br />\n(iii) A person or organization providing funds for the project.<br />\nNote : The project manager is appointed by the project sponsor and the project sponsor is appointed<br />\nby portfolio manager or CEO.</p>"},{"n":56,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The time-cost trade off figure outlines graphically four different time-cost positions A, B, C and D. Point ‘A’ represents normal time and normal cost.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f26dfdd68787044916d0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>Which of the following pairs is/are correctly matched?<br />\n1. Crashing all non-critical activities : Project will move to point ‘C’.<br />\n2. Crashing all the activities : Project will have to point ‘D’.<br />\n3. Crashing all critical activities : Project will move to point ‘B’.</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3"},{"key":"C","html":"3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ea/eadc9fdf1040903eaf35.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":57,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The interfering float of the activity shown below is</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bbb1d87a0d1c1b7aa153.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"-1"},{"key":"D","html":"2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/beb0ab27a91c692d28ab.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Match <strong>List-I</strong> (Curve) with <strong>List-II</strong> (Methods of depreciation) and select the correct answer using the codes given below the lists:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6eaf96600ccd4dc1eaa9.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":59,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The relative dielectric constant of a solid dielectric in alternating field is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"maximum at the power frequencies and decreases to unity at frequencies in the ultraviolet range."},{"key":"B","html":"maximum at power frequencies and decreases to zero at frequencies in the ultraviolet range."},{"key":"C","html":"unity at the power frequencies in the ultraviolet range."},{"key":"D","html":"independent of frequency variations."}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nAt low frequencies, ions have enough time to respond to the changing electric field. Hence, at<br />\nlow frequencies, all the four types of polarisations are present and the value of the total polarisation<br />\nis very high, leading to maximum value of &epsilon;<em><sub>r</sub></em> , and stop contributing to the total polarization. At<br />\nhigh frequencies, the Orientational and Ionic polorizations cannot keep up with the rapid field<br />\nreversa and mainly Electronic Polarization is present. Thus, the total polarization decreases leading<br />\nto &epsilon;<em><sub>r</sub></em> approaching unity at high frequencies. Therefore, the relative dielectric constant of a solid<br />\ndielectric in alternating field is maximum at the power frequencies and decreases to unity at<br />\nfrequencies in the ultraviolet range.</p>"},{"n":60,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Compared to other magnetic materials, a material with narrow hysteresis loop has</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"higher permeability, higher retentivity and higher coercivity."},{"key":"B","html":"higher permeability, lower retentivity and lower coercivity."},{"key":"C","html":"lower permeability, higher retentivity and lower reluctance."},{"key":"D","html":"lower permeability, lower retentivity and lower residual magnetism."}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fcb82549e53742aae1c3.png\" /></div>"},{"n":61,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements for <em>n</em>-type semiconductor<br />\n1. Fermi level lies below the donor level at room temperature <em>T</em>.<br />\n2. Fermi level lies above the donor level as <em>T</em> → 0.<br />\n3. Fermi level lies in valence band.<br />\n4. Fermi level remains invariant with temperature.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"2, 3 and 4 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3 only"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e8/e8130897d928591ca83f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. Electronic polarization increases due to increase in temperature.<br />\n2. Orientational polarization in dielectric is inversly proportional to temperature.<br />\nWhich of the above statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither 1 nor 2"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&bull; Electronic polarization is independent of temperature.<br />\n&bull; As temperature increases, the thermal motion of the molecules also increases, making it harder<br />\nfor the dipoles to align with the electric field. Thus, Orientational polarization in dielectric<br />\ndecreases with increase in temperature.<br />\nHence, only statement 2 is correct.</p>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements regarding magnetic materials:<br />\n1. Value of spontaneous magnetisation for a paramagnetic material is zero.<br />\n2. Diamagnetic materials have small permanent dipole moment.<br />\n3. In ferromagnetic materials, total magnetic flux density is summation of flux density due to applied field and flux density due to magnetization.<br />\nWhich of the above given statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 and 2 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 and 3 only"},{"key":"C","html":"1 and 3 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2 and 3"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; Diamagnetic materials do not have permanent dipole moment.<br />\n&bull; Paramagnetic materials do not exhibit spontaneous magnetization in the absence of an external<br />\nmagnetic field. Whereas Ferromagnetic materials exhibit spontaneous magnetization. We have,<br />\nB = &mu;<sub>0</sub>(H + M) i.e. for ferromagnetic materials, the total magnetic flux density is the summation<br />\nof the flux density due to the applied field (H) and the flux density due to the material&#39;s magnetization (M).<br />\nHence, statements 1 and 3 are correct.</p>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>“Manganin” an alloy of copper and manganese , is most prominently used in which of the following applications?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Heating elements manufacturing."},{"key":"B","html":"Ballast coils manufacturing."},{"key":"C","html":"Standard resistances manufacturing."},{"key":"D","html":"In candescant lamp manufacturing."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nManganin is an alloy of copper, manganese and nickel known for its low temperature coefficient<br />\nof resistance, high electrical resistivity, and low thermal EMF, making it ideal for use in precision<br />\nresistors. Thus, it is used as standard resistance manufacturing material. Standard resistances are<br />\nused for measurement purposes, etc.</p>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which material is used as transducer in working of microphone?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Conductors"},{"key":"B","html":"Dielectric"},{"key":"C","html":"Piezoelectric"},{"key":"D","html":"Insulator"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nPiezoelectric materials are used in microphone that convert sound energy (mechanical pressure<br />\nvariations from sound waves) into electrical signals.</p>"},{"n":66,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Hexagonal closed packed space lattice (HCP) is found in</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Zinc, Magnesium, Cobalt, Cadmium, Antimony and Bismuth"},{"key":"B","html":"Gamma-iron, Aluminium, Copper, Lead, Silver and Nickel"},{"key":"C","html":"Alpha-iron, Tungsten, Chromium and Molybdenum"},{"key":"D","html":"None of the above"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nClosed packed hexagonal space lattice (HCP) is found in Zinc, magnesium, cobalt, cadmium,<br />\nantimony and bismuth.</p>"},{"n":67,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Consider the following statements<br />\n1. Chain growth polymers are those polymers which are formed by successive addition of monomer units to the growing chain.<br />\n2. Chain growth polymers are formed by a process which involves chain reactions and the process is called chain growth polymerisation.<br />\nWhich of the statements is/are true?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"None the above"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nChain growth polymers are those polymers which are formed by successive addition of monomer<br />\nunits to the growing chain having a reactive intermediate (free radical, carbocation or carboanions)<br />\nat one end of the chain. The chain reaction process is called chain growth polymerization.</p>"},{"n":68,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The ultimate strength of a fibre is 1600 MPa, fibre diameter is 10 mm and shear strength between fibre and matrix is 100 MPa. What is the critical length of fibre ?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"100 μm"},{"key":"B","html":"80 μm"},{"key":"C","html":"40 μm"},{"key":"D","html":"160 μm"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2d/2d4745b19796996d79a6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":69,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The aluminium alloy made by melting aluminium with 2 to 10% magnesium and 1.75% copper is called</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Duralumin"},{"key":"B","html":"Y-alloy"},{"key":"C","html":"Magnalium"},{"key":"D","html":"Hindalium"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe aluminium alloy made by melting aluminium with 2 to 10% magnesium and 1.75% copper is<br />\ncalled magnalium. This alloy is known for its light weight and good mechanical properties, making<br />\nit suitable for use in aircraft and automobile components.</p>"},{"n":70,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Endurance limit is the primary concern in the design of<br />\n1. Rotating shaft<br />\n2. Machine base<br />\n3. Column<br />\n4. Industrial structure<br />\nWhich of the above is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"3 and 4 only"},{"key":"D","html":"1, 2, 3 and 4"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nEndurance limit is defined as the maximum stress level which when applied to a component for<br />\ninfinite number of loading and unloading cycles, will not result in a failure due to fatigue. Fatigue<br />\nis a failure when a component is subjected to fluctuating stress such as a rotating shaft. Whereas<br />\nMachine base, Column, and Industrial structure are primarily subjected to static or steady loads.</p>"},{"n":71,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Enviro-Bond polymer is used for water cleanup. Which of the following are correct about it?<br />\n1. It is hydrophobic in nature.<br />\n2. Its density is more than density of water.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"1 only"},{"key":"B","html":"2 only"},{"key":"C","html":"Both 1 and 2"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nEnviro-Bond polymer is used for water cleanup. It is hydrophobic (does not like water) and its<br />\ndensity is lower than the density of water so it float at the oil-water interface.<br />\nPolypropylene is also used for absorbing the oil from the ocean surface.</p>"},{"n":72,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A metal crystallizes in a face centred cubic structure. If the edge length of its unit cell is ‘a’, the closest approach between two atoms in metallic crystal will be:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e4/e4ac90c6623b59090db8.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/73/734162f8daeeb8e538ae.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"2<em>a</em>"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/46/46b15b9c4f3d0dd885ee.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/efa71fe60c5d0ac332ea.png\" /></div>"},{"n":73,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The system of equations</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/51/51aa15274964bcdb3346.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>has no solution if α is</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Either –2 or 1"},{"key":"B","html":"–2"},{"key":"C","html":"1"},{"key":"D","html":"Neither –2 nor 1"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/881dc07e2ef4c510ca1b.png\" /><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0348a1e7023085809e5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":74,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which of the following is an orthogonal matrix?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2e422c03a40b00aac7b4.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6fb5a2e358325c0daed7.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/66373a79744bdf4131ce.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/20/206f7e322653546c4dfb.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/19445cc39bce78c8691d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":75,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/a3/a37af888f15ea4d299d0.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/60/605ccde49e9dcb4dffee.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b16ad25dae18e859be3a.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/bb/bb6748bfa4733be65305.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/00/00b9f7203aac2c3d31a2.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fb/fb288e9f21776fa69529.png\" /></div>"},{"n":76,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p><img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/c7/c7dff8c81e6ed9cf0b97.png\" /></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"0"},{"key":"B","html":"1"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0e7ffde23c9ca25cad55.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/5402a1981a83a15845b7.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d18a424a23f32910be05.png\" /></div>"},{"n":77,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A signal which can be green or red with probability <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92eed1051d287cf58df7.png\" /> respectively, is received by station A and then transmitted to station B. The probability of each station receiving the signal correctly is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0ee52828cb1f2f016393.png\" /> If the signal received at station B is green, then the probability that the original signal was green is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2b/2b93ffd1422f4e9d5044.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/59/59d5ced9df6687fd95de.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/81/8190882b1a87a8c2a71a.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/febcecbadf7f6b494106.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/14/14ff860ee47a54334606.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d9338686aa380cde63e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":78,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A bag contains 4 red and 6 black balls. A ball is drawn at random from the bag, its colour is observed and this ball along with two additional balls of the same colour are returned to the bag. If now a ball is drawn at random from the bag, then the probability that this drawn ball is red, is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/41/41b240a880bdf2877bfa.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/37d843d3415c8d45c84d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6d/6d000f710557986a6aa8.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b5/b5caca45f9b55b7e2763.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/098b516dfaf7a658cfc5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":79,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>We wish to calculate the reciprocal value <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/55/5596ec868d051bce0e16.png\" /> by Newton-Raphson method for <em>f</em>(<em>x</em>) = 0. The Newton - Raphson algorithm (<em>x</em><sub><em>k</em>+1</sub>) for the function will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/3713161f56f3fede8036.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/89df4ae529dc07b8178d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/be/be1e057528db247e0832.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ba/ba4172ecd8fc6f7cc588.png\" />"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/379dd9a48e56528ffe1a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":80,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/f9/f9921dad653e8ece42de.png\" /> where <em>C</em> is a rectangle bounded by the lines x = ±a, y = 0, y = b is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2<em>a</em><sup>2</sup><em>b</em>"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/af81df290ac95eefcb02.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"–4a<em>b</em><sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"4<em>a</em><sup>2</sup><em>b</em>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/22/22c653a26e7459975c4a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a4f5963e8540865da593.png\" /></div>"},{"n":81,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>What is the remainder when<br />\n(1!)<sup>3</sup> + (2!)<sup>3</sup> + (3!)<sup>3</sup> + (4!)<sup>3</sup> + _______ (1152!)<sup>3</sup> is divided by 1152?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"125"},{"key":"B","html":"225"},{"key":"C","html":"325"},{"key":"D","html":"205"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a8/a8290b33e65f5492da6c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":82,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>We had 1000 goats at the beginning of year 2001 and the number of goats each year increases by 10% by giving birth (compounded annually). At the end of each year, we double the number of goats by purchasing the same no. of goats as there is the no. of goats with us at the time. What is the number of goats at the beginning of 2004?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"10600"},{"key":"B","html":"10648"},{"key":"C","html":"8848"},{"key":"D","html":"8226"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/64a72d66b111a594810d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":83,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A hemispherical bowl is filled to the brim with a beverage. The contents of the bowl are transferred into a cylindrical vessel whose radius is 50% more than its height. If the diameter is same for both the bowl and the cylinder, the volume of the beverage that can be poured in the cylindrical vessel is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21b7595a5d783166da46.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/641a005cf2e9dca05fb5.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"100%"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/26/26eb7f81e85c329565d9.png\" /></div>"},{"n":84,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A man and his wife appear in an interview for two vacancies in the same post. The probability of husband's selection is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2c/2c4849d18b53e1116222.png\" /> and the probability of wife’s selection is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/d8/d834bab89384d75d5e8a.png\" /> What is the probability that only one of them is selected?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/37094d5cb52d8ec38ae9.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8f/8f61ebdf97b6b6936c06.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f8544ffd18beb2d262ee.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8ee4f58804f811af0cc9.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d5e7693895e51a1147fd.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0ea889463e46e586eb58.png\" /></div>"},{"n":85,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>You have to study the question and all the three statements given to decide whether any information provided in the statement(s) is redundant and can be dispensed with while answering the given question.<br />\nAt what time will the train reach city X from city Y?<br />\nI. The train crosses another train of equal length of 200 metres and running in opposite direction in 15 seconds.<br />\nII. The train leaves city Y at 7.15 a.m. for city X situated at a distance of 558 km.<br />\nIII. The 200 metres long train crosses a signal pole in 10 seconds.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"I only"},{"key":"B","html":"II only"},{"key":"C","html":"III only"},{"key":"D","html":"I and III only"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/01/015f19b736f03082c7da.png\" /></div>"},{"n":86,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Read the following information carefully and answer the question given below :<br />\nPrashant Arora has three children - Sangeeta, Vimal and Ashish. Ashish married Monika, the eldest daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Roy. The Roys married their youngest daughter to the eldest son of Mr. and Mrs. Sharma, and they had two children named Amit and Shashi. The Roys have two more children, Roshan and Vandana, both elder to Veena. Sameer and Ajay are sons of Ashish and Monika. Rashmi is the daughter of Amit.<br />\nWhat is the surname of Rashmi?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Sharma"},{"key":"B","html":"Arora"},{"key":"C","html":"Roy"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nRashmi is the daughter of Amit, who is the eldest son of Sharmas and married to Veena, the<br />\nyoungest daughter of the Roys. So, the surname of Rashmi is Sharma. Hence, the answer is (a).</p>"},{"n":87,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Johnson left for his office in his car. He drove 15 km towards north and then 10 km towards west.<br />\nHe then turned to the south and covered 5 km. Further, he turned to the east and moved 8 km.<br />\nFinally, he turned right and drove 10 km. How far and in which direction is he from his starting point?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2 km West"},{"key":"B","html":"5 km East"},{"key":"C","html":"3 km North"},{"key":"D","html":"6 km South"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e3/e3b3f755311c2787383b.png\" /></div>"},{"n":88,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>At a farm, there are hens, cows and bullocks, and the keepers to look after them. There are 69 heads less than legs; the number of cows is double that of the bullocks; the number of cows and hens is the same and there is one keeper per ten birds and cattle. The total number of hens plus cows and bullocks, and their keepers does not exceed 50. How many cows are there?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"16"},{"key":"B","html":"14"},{"key":"C","html":"12"},{"key":"D","html":"10"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ba/ba039fee25fd0248e6aa.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5bcc76e4c44847585c8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":89,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For past 2 years, the price of Harley motorcycles remained the same. Because of new tariffs imposed by Trump, the price of motorcycle increased by 50% last week, and stayed at this new level. This week, Narendra purchased the motorcycle with a 50% discount coupon. Narendra paid <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/37/37411bd13f6eb798942d.png\" /> What was the original price, before last week’s price increase?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fc/fce18720977c822236e3.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7c/7c946dc66a88c68c4950.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/af/afbd5435747bff04ed16.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/52/523538befda18635cca9.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8d51c34dc30a40151c7c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":90,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Varun saves 10% of his income. But when his income increases by 20% after 2 years still he saves 10% of his previous income. Then by how much percentage has his expenditure increased?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"20%"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/71/71c78a9000b14a15dca6.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/68cd3f56580a7db7cd76.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"22%"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae2964db4f68c93c5002.png\" /></div>"},{"n":91,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I)</strong> As the number of backup components increase the reliability of the system increases.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> Backup component have maximum value of reliability which is equal to the main component reliability.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nBoth are the correct individually, as increasing the backup component in the case of parallel<br />\nconnection Reliability is always increase. Reason is individually true, because this the feature of<br />\nbackup component.</p>"},{"n":92,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I) :</strong> Single stroke lettering is just freehand writing.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> Single stroke lettering is done without lifting the pencil.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nSingle stroke means the thickness of letters should be uniform.<br />\nThe letter is made of one or more stems or curves, each of which is made of a single stroke. It<br />\ndoes not mean that pencil will not be lifted during lettering.</p>"},{"n":93,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I) :</strong> Kernel is the core component of the operating system that interacts directly with the hardware.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II) :</strong> Kernel in Operating System is implemented using Machine Level Language (MLL).</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; Kernel is the core component of the operating system that interacts directly with the hardware.<br />\nThe Kernel mode is also called Central Mode or Privileged Mode, and taken as Master Program<br />\nstaying close to Hardware and regulating its use. In Kernel mode, the executing code has<br />\ncomplete and unrestricted access to the underlying hardware.<br />\n&bull; Kernel is typically implemented using a combination of high-level and low-level programming<br />\nlanguages such as C and assembly, not strictly machine language. Hence, Statement (II) is<br />\nfalse.</p>"},{"n":94,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I) :</strong> ICT in education blends technology with the conventional classroom teachinglearning process.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II) :</strong> ICT learning promotes a single pedagogy in learning which involves thematic integrative approach.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nICT learning promotes multiple pedagogy in learning like thematic integrative approach, creative<br />\nlearning, collaborative learning, active learning, etc.</p>"},{"n":95,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> When the soil becomes dry, the capability of the plants to act as carbon sink reduces.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> With increase in soil temperature, the microorganisms in dry soil become more productive.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":96,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> Producers are also known as autotrophs or self-feeders.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> Producers manufacture the organic compounds that they use as a source of energy and nutrients.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":97,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> Ethical theories must be sufficiently comprehensive to provide guidance in specific situation of interests to us.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> It must not be compatible with our most carefully considered moral convictions about concrete situations.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>"},{"n":98,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> A code of conduct is a set of values, rules, standards, and principles outlining what employers expect from staff within an organization.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> Codes of conduct are primarily formulated for self-interest.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":99,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> Disaster Risk Index (DRI) covers hazards, vulnerabilities, and exposures, with population and GDP being the two main exposure parameters.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> This index was developed by the 15th Finance Commission to bring objectivity in fiscal federalism by taking note of disaster risk faced by states for resource allocation.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\n&bull; The Disaster Risk Index (DRI) was developed by the 15th Finance Commission to bring<br />\nobjectivity in fiscal federalism by taking note of disaster risk faced by states for resource allocation.<br />\n&bull; The DRI covers 14 hazards (such as earthquake, cyclone, flood, drought), 14 vulnerabilities<br />\n(like rural/ urban poor, vulnerable children and women), and 2 exposure parameters - population and GDP.</p>"},{"n":100,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • ELECTRONICS ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Each of the next items consists of two statements, one labelled as the ‘Statement (I)’ and the other as ‘Statement (II)’. You are to examine these two statements carefully and select the answers to these items using the codes given below:<br />\n<strong>Codes:</strong><br />\n(a) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true and Statement (II) is the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(b) Both Statement (I) and Statement (II) are individually true but Statement (II) is NOT the correct explanation of Statement (I).<br />\n(c) Statement (I) is true but Statement (II) is false.<br />\n(d) Statement (I) is false but Statement (II) is true.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Statement (I):</strong> H-1B visa is designed to fill specialised skill gaps in the US labour market where qualified Americans are unavailable.<br />\n<strong>Statement (II):</strong> China is the biggest beneficiary of the H-1B program followed by India.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"a"},{"key":"B","html":"b"},{"key":"C","html":"c"},{"key":"D","html":"d"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\n&bull; An H-1B visa is a non-immigrant visa in the United States that allows US companies to<br />\ntemporarily employ foreign workers in specialty occupations. These are jobs that typically<br />\nrequire technical expertise, a bachelor&rsquo;s degree or higher, or its equivalent in fields like IT,<br />\nengineering, science, medicine, and finance.<br />\n&bull; It is designed to fill specialised skill gaps in the US labor market where qualified Americans are unavailable.<br />\n&bull; Indians have been the biggest beneficiaries of the H-1B program, accounting for more than<br />\n70% of successful H-1B petitions followed by China, who account for 12-13%.</p>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"Technical","start":0,"count":100}],"stats":{"questions":100,"maxMarks":200,"types":{"MCQ":99,"MSQ":1},"withoutKey":0}};
